{"step_index":493,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-16T19:02:10Z","input_tokens":2957,"cache_read_tokens":94859,"output_tokens":974,"thinking":"Adding per-step CPU/RAM columns to the main results file will provide granular resource usage data alongside overall performance metrics. Exporting a long-format resource file facilitates easier visualization of resource trends across scenarios and steps. Also, including the raw data allows for further investigation or alternative analysis methods.\n\n\nConsidering concurrent verification, the rapid deletion of Team 1's containers could interfere with Team 8's still-in-progress cloning process if they share resources. This timing introduces a potential race condition where resources are released and re-allocated under high contention. Verify needs a mechanism to ensure resource isolation and prevent deletion of resources still in use by another concurrent task.\n\n\nThe current sampling window is too short to capture the concurrent state, as container lifespans are brief relative to the sampling interval. Extending the container's active duration during verification would significantly increase the overlap for concurrent sampling. Alternatively, precise timestamp recording could facilitate a more accurate analysis of concurrency without modifying container lifespans.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"ask_question","args":{"questions":[{"is_multi_select":false,"options":["(Recommended) Keep the command identical across Alpine and Ubuntu for a strict apples-to-apples comparison, and add a 2-second hold (sh -c 'sleep 2 && echo verified') on the first container so clones stay alive simultaneously for ≥20 sampler ticks (2.0s) before cleanup starts","Keep 'echo verified_appX' with zero sleep (fastest possible execution, even if Verify Execution only lasts ~100-300ms per team)","For Ubuntu Heavy, also check that nginx/postgresql are running inside the container during verification"],"question":"5. Because 'echo verified' finishes in ~0.1s and immediately triggers clone deletion, fast teams can delete their clones before slower teams finish cloning. How should Verify Execution behave so we capture true peak RAM when all 2*M*N containers are alive?"}],"toolAction":"Asking Question 5 on Verify Execution hold for true peak RAM capture","toolSummary":"Ask Question 5: Capturing peak RAM during Verify Execution"}}]}
